# Release notes

When cutting a GitHub release for this plugin (`gh release create` / editing release body):

1. Bump `version` in `orca-plugin.json` and `src/version.ts`, commit, push `main`, tag `v<version>`, push the tag.
2. In the release notes body, always include an **Update** section with the exact terminal commands pinned to that tag.

Catalog installs (`aywengo.omlx` from `orca-community-plugins`) cannot be overwritten by a Git URL. Release notes must tell people to uninstall the catalog copy first, then install the tag:

```markdown
## Update

If you installed from the community catalog, remove that copy first, then install this tag:

```sh
orca plugin uninstall aywengo.omlx
orca plugin install aywengo/orca-mlx-plugin@vX.Y.Z
```

If Orca asks for approval, re-run the install command with the `--approve …` fingerprint it prints.
```

Replace `vX.Y.Z` with the tag for that release (e.g. `v1.2.0`). Do not omit the `@v…` ref.

Do not present bare `orca plugin install …@v…` alone as the only step — catalog users hit “remove it first”.
